  const olympusNpcs = [{"key":"calliope","name":"Calliope","title":"Muse of the Open Gate","role":"Narrator","x":50,"y":48,"info":"A silver-voiced muse who records the first mortals to step from Veyra into Olympus. She introduces the divine domains and the daily descent of bosses.","portrait":"/images/npcs/Calliope_portrait.webp","marker":"/images/npcs/Calliope_marker.webp","midjourney_prompt":"Calliope muse of epic poetry, female Greek myth narrator, silver laurel crown, white and gold robes, glowing scroll, standing before a celestial gate to Olympus, anime fantasy game NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed costume and shoulders, no full body, no cropped head, ornate divine background, soft cinematic light, highly detailed --ar 2:3 --v 6","portrait_prompt":"Calliope muse of epic poetry, female Greek myth narrator, silver laurel crown, white and gold robes, glowing scroll, standing before a celestial gate to Olympus, anime fantasy game NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed costume and shoulders, no full body, no cropped head, ornate divine background, soft cinematic light, highly detailed --ar 2:3 --v 6","marker_prompt":"small circular fantasy map marker icon for Calliope, silver muse mask and glowing scroll, white gold laurel, Olympus blue-gold aura, clean readable silhouette, transparent background, game UI icon --ar 1:1 --v 6","intro_dialogue":["Did you just come out of the gate?! By the Muses... a mortal road has truly reached Olympus.","Listen carefully. This realm is not one kingdom. It is a wheel of divine domains, each ruled by a divinity, each shaped by their nature.","There are eight great domains across Olympus, and beneath them lies a ninth forbidden place: Tartarus, the prison-domain where the Titans are chained.","A divine boss descends into one domain each day. The order is hidden from mortals, but the cycle never stops. Watch the skies, read the omens, and choose your route wisely.","If you survive these roads, your world will learn why the divinities sealed this place from ordinary maps."],"random_dialogue":true,"dialogue":["The clouds are quieter today. That is rarely a mercy in Olympus.","If a statue turns its head to watch you, bow first and panic second.","Hermes leaves messages in footprints. Unfortunately, he also lies with excellent handwriting.","The divinities love symbols. If a road shines too brightly, assume it wants something from you.","Tartarus is not beneath Olympus in the ordinary sense. It is beneath the rules.","Do not ask me for the boss order. Prophecy dislikes being treated like a schedule.","A mortal who survives a divine domain becomes a rumor. Survive two, and the divine court begins using your name carefully.","Apollo calls his domain a sanctuary. His enemies usually call it their last sunrise.","Athena respects preparation more than bravery. Bring both, but lead with preparation.","Ares does not test whether you can win. He tests what you become when winning hurts.","Poseidon smiles like the sea: beautiful from far away, fatal up close.","Hera keeps records of every broken oath. Try not to become fresh ink.","Artemis hears careless footsteps before the foot knows it has landed.","Zeus is not the storm. He is the pause before it decides where to fall.","The Titans remember a world before names. That is why their prison has so many locks.","Olympus lets mortals in only when Olympus needs something. Remember that.","If you hear singing from an empty bridge, do not answer in rhyme.","A divine boss descends daily, but the real danger is the domain learning how you fight.","Carry questions, not certainty. Certainty gets heavy on holy roads.","You came through a gate. That means someone, somewhere, failed to keep it closed."]},{"key":"brontes","name":"Brontes","title":"Cyclops of the Third Anvil","role":"Legendary Fusion Blacksmith","shop":"brontes_mythic_forge","x":65,"y":35,"info":"A one-eyed divine smith descended from the Cyclopes who forged thunder. His forge creates Mythic gear by making an Olympian legendary devour another level 5 legendary of the same type.","portrait":"/images/npcs/Brontes_portrait.webp","marker":"/images/npcs/Brontes_marker.webp","midjourney_prompt":"Brontes cyclops blacksmith from Greek mythology, one glowing eye, massive bronze hammer, divine forge sparks, Olympus anvil, molten gold and thunder metal, muscular fantasy NPC, anime game character portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed leather apron, shoulders and forge scars, no full body, no cropped head, dramatic rim light --ar 2:3 --v 6","portrait_prompt":"Brontes cyclops blacksmith from Greek mythology, one glowing eye, massive bronze hammer, divine forge sparks, Olympus anvil, molten gold and thunder metal, muscular fantasy NPC, anime game character portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed leather apron, shoulders and forge scars, no full body, no cropped head, dramatic rim light --ar 2:3 --v 6","marker_prompt":"small circular fantasy map marker icon for Brontes, single cyclops eye above crossed hammer and anvil, molten gold sparks, bronze forge rim, transparent background, game UI icon --ar 1:1 --v 6","dialogue":["Hah. I smell mortal steel and borrowed luck. Good. Luck melts quickly.","A normal legendary can climb to level 5 and call itself complete. My anvil disagrees.","Bring me a level 5 Olympian legendary equipment or weapon, and another level 5 legendary of the same type: helmet, armor, gloves, boots, weapon, or class weapon.","The Olympian legend will devour the other. The sacrifice is gone forever, but its effect is hammered into the surviving item.","What remains is beyond legendary: Mythic. Higher stats than a normal level 5 legendary, carrying both stories: the Olympian effect and the devoured legendary effect.","The forge fee is 500,000,000 gold. If your hand trembles, good. That means you understand the cost."]},{"key":"melanippe","name":"Melanippe","title":"Keeper of Areion Stables","role":"Pet Armor and Mount Upgrades","shop":"melanippe_stable","x":42,"y":40,"info":"A horse-master named for the old Greek line of warrior women. She tends the immortal bloodline of Areion and will sell pet armor and stable upgrades.","portrait":"/images/npcs/Melanippe_portrait.webp","marker":"/images/npcs/Melanippe_marker.webp","midjourney_prompt":"Melanippe Greek myth stable keeper, warrior horsewoman, celestial stables of Areion, bronze bridle, white immortal horse armor, blue and gold Olympus city, anime fantasy NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed riding cloak, shoulders and bronze stable gear, no full body, no cropped head, elegant confident expression --ar 2:3 --v 6","portrait_prompt":"Melanippe Greek myth stable keeper, warrior horsewoman, celestial stables of Areion, bronze bridle, white immortal horse armor, blue and gold Olympus city, anime fantasy NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed riding cloak, shoulders and bronze stable gear, no full body, no cropped head, elegant confident expression --ar 2:3 --v 6","marker_prompt":"small circular fantasy map marker icon for Melanippe, winged horse bridle and polished pet armor plate, blue-white stable aura, gold trim, transparent background, game UI icon --ar 1:1 --v 6","dialogue":["Careful where you step. Divine horses bite harder than most monsters.","Bring a Hermes Core if you want access to my stable shelves. I do not armor companions for tourists.","I can bind sigils to your pets: one for attack, one for defense. Copies matter; one sigil copy can serve one pet.","A pet is not decoration in Olympus. It is the difference between reaching the next bridge and becoming a cautionary song."]},{"key":"melinoe","name":"Melinoe","title":"Night Egg Envoy","role":"Limited Rare Pet Eggs","x":45,"y":60,"info":"A veiled underworld wanderer tied to nightmares and moonlit crossroads. She will appear with limited-time rare pet eggs and strange promotional offers.","portrait":"/images/npcs/Melinoe_portrait.webp","marker":"/images/npcs/Melinoe_marker.webp","midjourney_prompt":"Melinoe Greek underworld goddess inspired dark elf envoy, half moonlit half shadow face, violet-black robes, rare glowing monster eggs, Tartarus chains in background, mysterious fantasy anime NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed veil, shoulders and jeweled collar, no full body, no cropped head --ar 2:3 --v 6","portrait_prompt":"Melinoe Greek underworld goddess inspired dark elf envoy, half moonlit half shadow face, violet-black robes, rare glowing monster eggs, Tartarus chains in background, mysterious fantasy anime NPC portrait from chest to head, centered upper-body composition, face clearly visible, detailed veil, shoulders and jeweled collar, no full body, no cropped head --ar 2:3 --v 6","marker_prompt":"small circular fantasy map marker icon for Melinoe, violet rare pet egg with crescent moon crack, dark elf veil silhouette, black-purple glow, transparent background, game UI icon --ar 1:1 --v 6","dialogue":["Do not stare too long at the eggs. Some things stare back before they hatch.","My stock changes when the underworld opens its eye. Rare companions, brief chances, no second knocks.","If you hear scratching from inside the shell, that is usually a good sign. Usually."]},{"key":"damon","name":"Damon","title":"Apothecary of Epidaurus","role":"Potion Merchant","shop":"damon_potions","x":69,"y":52,"info":"A human healer trained in the sanctuary traditions of Asclepius. He sells potions brewed for mortals who insist on fighting divine things.","portrait":"/images/npcs/Damon_portrait.webp","marker":"/images/npcs/Damon_marker.webp","midjourney_prompt":"Damon human Greek apothecary, Asclepiu